        en: {
            eyebrow: `Eureka Express · The Legacy`,
            title: `The Legacy`,
            subtitle: `The family foundation gives a lot and changes little. You are its first professional director and you have four board meetings, one each December, to turn it into something the family can look at with pride and the figures can prove.`,
            period_label: `Block`,
            period_of: `of`,
            kpi_score: `Score`,
            kpi_of100: `/100`,
            kpi_out: `Verified outcomes`,
            kpi_out_unit: `people with a checked outcome between 2026 and 2030: young people in skilled work, older people still safely at home`,
            kpi_cpo: `Cost per outcome`,
            kpi_cpo_unit: `everything the foundation spends divided by the outcomes (about €28,900 in 2026)`,
            kpi_given: `Euros to programmes`,
            kpi_given_unit: `what reaches organisations, scholarships and buildings between 2026 and 2030`,
            kpi_health: `Grantee health`,
            kpi_health_unit: `0 to 100: whether the organisations you fund come out stronger or weaker`,
            kpi_coh: `Family cohesion`,
            kpi_coh_unit: `0 to 100: whether the family, from Julián to the cousins, feels the foundation is theirs`,
            kpi_gov: `Governance and transparency`,
            kpi_gov_unit: `0 to 100: independence, conflicts of interest handled properly and clear accounts`,
            briefing_label: `Situation`,
            r1_name: `Board meeting of 15 December 2026 · Purpose and governance`,
            r2_name: `Board meeting of 14 December 2027 · How the money is given`,
            r3_name: `Board meeting of 12 December 2028 · Measure and report`,
            r4_name: `Board meeting of 11 December 2029 · The next generation`,
            round_done: `Five grant years closed`,
            r1_brief: `Monday 14 December 2026. Two weeks ago you became the first executive director of the Recuero Foundation, which your father, Julián, set up in 2009 with 8% of Recuero Envases and a financial portfolio: about 24 million euros yielding 1.1 million net a year. The 2026 report is in front of you: €950,000 spread over 61 donations of about €15,600 to causes the trustees proposed, and €120,000 for the Recuero Gala in June. The only thing anyone can count is about 38 people with a checked outcome: almost €28,900 of spending per outcome. Tomorrow the board, four family members, decides the policy for 2027. Start with the basics: what the foundation is for, who governs it and what you do with the 61 usual donations.`,
            r2_brief: `December 2027. The foundation now runs on your first design. Now you decide how the money is given. Until now almost everything has been one-year grants for the costs of a specific project, to organisations the trustees propose; the organisations say they cannot hire or plan with money that expires in twelve months. And Mikel, your brother and a trustee, offers his office building in Alcalá as headquarters for €4,000 a month; similar offices rent for about €30,000 a year. Decide the form of the grant, how grantees are chosen and what you do with Mikel's offer.`,
            r3_brief: `December 2028. The board wants to know what has been achieved, and the foundation can only count euros handed out, events and press cuttings. The Recuero Gala in June costs €120,000 a year. And your father, Julián, turning 81, asks for 1.5 million euros for a Julián Recuero Auditorium at the vocational training school of Azuqueca: €600,000 a year from the grant budget in 2029 and 2030 and another €300,000 a year from the endowment. Decide what is measured, what the foundation tells the world and what you do with the auditorium.`,
            r4_brief: `December 2029. Recuero Envases has lost its largest customer and will pay no dividend in 2030: with the portfolio yielding less, 2030 net income falls to about €770,000, €330,000 less. Mikel proposes that the family holding buy the foundation's 8% stake at book value, 1.95 million against an appraisal of 3.25 million. Two of the seven fourth-generation cousins, aged 18 to 30, have also asked to join the foundation, and the board must decide how it renews itself from 2030. Decide what you do about the cousins, the 2030 gap and the board.`,
            brief_done: `The five grant years are closed. Review the final summary and the history table.`,
            r1_heading: `Block 1 · Purpose and governance`,
            r1_intro: `What you decide here applies from 2027. Until you decide the next blocks, the calculation assumes the options pre-selected in them: one-year grants, organisations proposed by the trustees and staying in the company's room; counting euros, the gala and building the auditorium; leaving the cousins out, cutting in proportion in 2030 and trustees for life.`,
            r2_heading: `Block 2 · How the money is given`,
            r2_intro: `What you decide here applies from 2028. Mikel's building, if leased, is paid from 2028.`,
            r3_heading: `Block 3 · Measure and report`,
