            fb_r1_company: `Moving the giving into the company makes it cheaper and turns it into marketing: the chief executive decides, the foundation's own governance disappears and the family stops feeling the foundation is theirs.`,
            fb_r1_name: `The Recuero Prize is visible and focused on the wrong thing: on the family, not on a problem. Each euro of the prize buys very few outcomes.`,
            fb_r1_cut: `Stopping the 61 donations on 1 January frees money at once and leaves organisations that relied on it without notice; and the new strategy needs a year to find whom to work with.`,
            fb_r1_scatter: `Keeping what the trustees propose keeps the peace at the table and the foundation without a focus: nobody can learn, choose well or account for sixty different causes.`,
            fb_r1_keep: `Keeping the 61 donations leaves half of every budget where it was: the focus is well chosen, but there is no money left to run it.`,
            fb_r1_family: `A family-only board can work, but with nobody from outside and no conflicts policy every decision depends on the goodwill of whoever sits at the table.`,
            fb_r1_ok: `Two areas with a theory of change, two independent trustees with a conflicts policy, and an orderly exit from the old donations: the foundation now has a purpose and governance.`,
            fb_r2_approve: `Mikel is pleased and the office is ready. But a trustee who contracts with the foundation needs the Protectorate's prior authorisation (art. 28 of Ley 50/2002), and he also votes on his own matter.`,
            fb_r2_friends: `The organisations the trustees bring are their friends': without published criteria, selection is a permanent conflict of interest and chooses worse.`,
            fb_r2_small: `One-year project grants feed the starvation cycle: the organisation cannot pay the people who do the work or plan beyond twelve months.`,
            fb_r2_heavy: `A 40-page form for a €20,000 grant spends the organisation's money on paperwork and the foundation's on reviewing it, without choosing better than a light process.`,
            fb_r2_match: `Grants conditional on raising the same amount elsewhere push the fundraising burden onto small organisations with nobody to do it.`,
            fb_r2_wait: `Staying in the company's room is free and postpones the problem: the foundation depends on the company and Mikel's matter stays on the table without a procedure.`,
            fb_r2_ok: `Three-year grants for the organisation's operations, proportionate selection and Mikel's conflict handled by procedure: the foundation gives better and protects itself.`,
            fb_r3_count: `Counting euros, events and press cuttings measures the foundation, not the people it serves; without outcomes there is no way to learn what works.`,
            fb_r3_silent: `Saying nothing saves the gala and leaves the foundation unaccountable: neither the family nor the territory knows what is done with the money.`,
            fb_r3_refuse: `Turning the auditorium down at the board saves money and hurts Julián in front of his family: cohesion collapses over a decision that could have been redesigned with him.`,
            fb_r3_build: `The auditorium honours Julián and eats two years of grants: 1.5 million euros in bricks produce very few outcomes for people.`,
            fb_r3_audit: `An external evaluation of every grant measures rigorously and costs 15% of every euro, and exhausts small organisations: measurement has to be proportionate.`,
            fb_r3_gala: `The gala brings the family together one night a year and costs €120,000; it tells who was there, not what changed.`,
            fb_r3_ok: `Agreed outcome indicators, a report that also tells what did not work, and Julián's wish turned into scholarships the school needs: the foundation now knows what it achieves.`,
            fb_r4_sell: `The sale covers the gap and keeps the shares in the family. But selling endowment assets needs the Protectorate's authorisation (art. 21) and buyer and seller are the same trustees (art. 28): 1.3 million euros pass from the foundation to the family.`,
            fb_r4_ceo: `Having the chief executive chair the foundation ties it to the company's communication: less independence, worse decisions and a family that sees it as one more department.`,
